* VARIABLE: 
\b Avg_CG_Transfers
\b0  Average yearly fiscal transfers (
\i Fonds de Dotation de la D\'e9centralisation
\i0 ) in dollars from the central government to a rural community, 2009-12\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \ul \ulc0 Source\ulnone : Direction des Collectivities Locales\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b CR_2002_num / CR_2009_num / CR_2012_num 
\b0 Number assigned to each 
\i communaut\'e9 rurale
\i0  or local government (villages are nested in local governments) existing in 2002, 2009 and 2012 respectively\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Centr_DiscountRate_20km
\b0  A discount-decay function of an area's level of centralization at 8 time periods between 1500-1880 Areas are coded as centralized 0-1 for each time period based on whether or not they fall within a 20km buffer of a pre-colonial capital or key city\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Ch_Teacher_Student_Ratio_T1
\b0  / 
\b Ch_Teacher_Student_Ratio_T2
\b0  The number of new, central-state appointed teachers assigned to a region per student-aged capita between 2002-09 / 2009-12; measure is standardized to a 0-1 scale\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruence_20km_CRavg_T1
\b0  / 
\b Congruence_20km_CRavg_T2
\b0  Average congruence score (Congruence_20km_T1
\b ) 
\b0 by local government for each time period\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruence_20km_Regavg_T1
\b0  / 
\b Congruence_20km_Regavg_T2
\b0  Average congruence score (Congruence_20km_T1
\b ) 
\b0 by region for each time period\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruence_20km_T1 /  Congruence_20km_T2 
\b0 A discount-decay function of a village's congruence with the dominant level of precolonial centralization in the local government, thus that a village receives a 1 if it is 'congruent' and a 0 if not; coded by time period with centralization measured as a 20km buffer from a key precolonial power center\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruence_25km_T1 /  Congruence_25km_T2 
\b0 A discount-decay function of a village's congruence with the dominant level of precolonial centralization in the local government, thus that a village receives a 1 if it is 'congruent' and a 0 if not; coded by time period with centralization measured as a 25km buffer from a key precolonial power center\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruence_30km_T1 /  Congruence_30km_T2 
\b0 A discount-decay function of a village's congruence with the dominant level of precolonial centralization in the local government, thus that a village receives a 1 if it is 'congruent' and a 0 if not; coded by time period with centralization measured as a 30km buffer from a key precolonial power center\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruence_Index_20km
\b0  / 
\b Congruence_Index_25km
\b0  / 
\b Congruence_Index_30km
\b0  Bockstette, Chanda and Putterman's (2002) state antiquity index with a discount-decay function All variables within 20, 25 and 30km of pre-colonial capitals are assigned the score for the level of 'statehood' of a kingdom at 8 time periods between 1500-1880 \
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruent_25_Dummy_T1
\b0  / 
\b Congruent_25_Dummy_T2
\b0  / 
\b Congruent_30_Dummy_T1
\b0  / 
\b Congruent_30_Dummy_T2
\b0   A 0-1 measure where villages take a value of 1 if they fall within the 25 or 30km buffer of an area that was centralized in 1880\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Congruent_Dummy_2002
\b0  / 
\b Congruent_Dummy_2009
\b0  A 0-1 measure where villages take a value of 1 if it was congruent with a 20km buffer of an area that was centralized in 1880\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded, misc historical sources\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b D_Clinic_09_sqrt
\b0  Square root of the minimum distance to the nearest clinic from a given village in 2009\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded; Senegalese Ministry of Health\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b D_School_02_sqrt
\b0  / 
\b D_School_09_sqrt
\b0  Square root of the minimum distance to the nearest school from a given village in 2002 / 2009\
\ul Source\ulnone : Author coded; Senegalese Ministry of Education\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b Department_2002 / Department_2009 
\b0 The Department (second-level administrative unit) that the local government falls within in 2002 or 2009 respectively\
\
* VARIABLE: 
\b ELF_Arr_02
\b0  / 
\b ELF_Arr_09
